WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.654
"To put numbers on it: a NeuPL population capped at
eight policies beats PSRO populations

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:10.099
of eight policies even when PSRO trained twice as
long per iteration.

00:00:10.179 --> 00:00:12.804
As relative population performance climbs,

00:00:12.884 --> 00:00:17.121
the effective number of distinct policies grows
from five to eight,

00:00:17.201 --> 00:00:22.081
and across different maximum caps the effective
size saturates around twelve.

00:00:22.161 --> 00:00:26.849
The transfer study spans Nash mixtures over two,
four, and seven policies,

00:00:26.929 --> 00:00:28.459
each repeated five times.

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:35.610
Together these establish NeuPL as more
sample-efficient and more robust than the standard iterative baselines."
